| **Chavín de Huántar galleries** | Gallery-filtered pututu spectra; Lanzón→Circular Plaza transmission (site-specific Hz in dissertation) | Lanzón Gallery, Circular Plaza | Calibrated sources/mics, impulse responses, auralization | Abel et al. 2008 (JASA 123:605); Kolar 2013 PhD, Stanford CCRMA; https://ccrma.stanford.edu/groups/chavin/ |
| **Le Portel / Niaux / Isturitz caves** | Resonant pitches mapped as notes (E2–F–B2 region), **3–4 s resonance durations** at painted loci | Gallery Jammes (Le Portel) etc. | Vocal pitch survey (uncalibrated) | Reznikoff & Dauvois 1988, BSPF 85(8):238–246 |

**Matching-study caveats (apply before correlating with cymatic decodes):**
1. The 95–120 Hz "megalithic band" is what the wave equation *predicts* for 2–3 m stone cavities (f ≈ c/2L ⇒ ~57–86 Hz for 2–3 m axial modes, higher for transverse). A match between a crop-circle "decode" and 110 Hz has very low evidentiary weight — the band is densely populated by any human-scale chamber.
2. Use only swept-sine/ISO-calibrated Hz (Jahn et al. 1996; Till 2017; Cox et al. 2020) as ground truth. Voice/drum-excited peaks (Debertolis; Reznikoff) carry excitation bias.
3. "110 Hz at the Hypogeum" is a meme, not a measurement — the site's calibrated modes are 41/72/76 Hz.

